WEBVTT

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:05.920
Date Masamune.

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:08.660
We've been told to find her.

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:12.470
She escaped from prison 
and is still on the run.

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:15.450
We cannot leave her.

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:18.690
Do I have to handle this?

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:22.390
You know her well, Higurashi-kun.

00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:24.830
Don't say it like that, it's creepy.

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:31.920
<b>Chief</b>

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:29.520
I just found her and 
threw her in prison.

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:32.090
But you found her interesting, right?

00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:34.060
Sure.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:36.210
But you'd need more lives than

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:38.970
a cat to go after her and survive.

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:40.990
Correct.

00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:45.980
But you know what this place is, right?

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:48.170
The Warring States General 
Countermeasures Department,

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:49.440
AKA WarGen.

00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:51.790
The place where we handle incidents

00:00:51.790 --> 00:00:53.760
caused by warring states generals.

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:55.100
Then you understand why

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:59.660
you have to chase the 
escapee Date Masamune.

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:03.310
Can I start tomorrow?

00:01:03.310 --> 00:01:04.520
Start today.

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:06.490
And I'm assigning you a new partner.

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:10.610
I told you we were getting someone new.

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:11.920
You did.

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:15.200
A warring states general 
who wanted to help us.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:16.920
Her name was the same

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:20.510
as the leader of the 
Green Gang, Katakura...

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:24.060
See? Beautiful isn't she?

00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:27.960
Katakura Kojuro.

00:01:30.310 --> 00:01:33.350
Nice to meet you, Higurashi-san.

00:03:12.310 --> 00:03:15.040
We've been instructed to 
follow Date Masamune's

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:17.460
trail from the beginning again.

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:19.040
So I've been told.

00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:23.350
You've completely lost track 
of her, haven't you?

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:26.000
Try too hard

00:03:27.320 --> 00:03:28.980
and you'll get hurt.

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:33.100
Some things are best 
not to pursue too hard.

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:37.150
But isn't that your job 
as a police officer?

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:41.570
That's why we have to chase her.

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:45.800
You were her teacher, right?

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:47.480
Any ideas?

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:49.280
None, especially.

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:52.580
I'd like to check this again.

00:03:53.270 --> 00:03:56.750
Do you really plan to catch her?

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:58.000
Of course.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:00.950
I'd like to think I've done everything 
I can for that to happen.

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:05.240
Otherwise you wouldn't be 
allowed into WarGen, yeah.

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:06.010
Yes.

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:09.850
You're a cold person.

00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:16.220
Then would you rather I met 
up with her and ran away?

00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:20.230
Masamune-san wouldn't 
be so lonely then.

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:21.870
Answer me seriously.

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:25.360
You could, but you'd 
get caught eventually.

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:27.350
Even if you weren't,

00:04:27.350 --> 00:04:30.090
you could never forget 
you were being hunted.

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:31.520
True.

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:37.130
Then what's wrong with 
me helping the police?

00:04:37.530 --> 00:04:38.710
Nothing's wrong.

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:40.590
You're doing the right thing.

00:04:41.570 --> 00:04:43.850
But sometimes even if it's 
the right thing to do,

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:45.070
people can't do it.

00:04:45.070 --> 00:04:46.890
I don't believe so.

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:51.000
Anyone who's committed a 
crime must be punished,

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:54.850
even, no, especially 
if they're close to me.

00:04:55.270 --> 00:04:58.050
That's one way to look at things.

00:05:00.090 --> 00:05:01.960
I'll do my job.

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:03.360
I hope so.

00:05:03.850 --> 00:05:05.700
Of course I will.

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:08.720
Did you forget what our 
department is called?

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:13.870
The Warring States General 
Countermeasures Department, yes?

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:35.380
Masamune-san saved me 
when I was being hassled

00:05:35.380 --> 00:05:37.100
by a group of teenage thugs.

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:39.280
That's news to me.

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:41.910
So she's assaulting minors now?

00:05:42.580 --> 00:05:44.870
Were you listening to me?

00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:47.340
She saved me!

00:05:48.060 --> 00:05:51.590
The police wouldn't help, but you're

00:05:51.590 --> 00:05:54.330
going to arrest her, anyway?

00:05:55.140 --> 00:05:57.250
This is above my pay grade.

00:05:58.140 --> 00:06:01.000
Once we catch her you 
can talk to the judge.

00:06:03.640 --> 00:06:05.510
Two coffees, yes?

00:06:09.010 --> 00:06:11.390
I don't think you should be staring

00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:13.020
at girls as they walk away.

00:06:13.020 --> 00:06:14.810
You're right.

00:06:15.630 --> 00:06:20.030
Honestly, I didn't think 
she'd be this easy to track.

00:06:20.030 --> 00:06:23.570
What have the police here been doing?

00:06:25.010 --> 00:06:28.790
Anyway, I guess your old student
is an interesting person.

00:06:28.790 --> 00:06:30.290
What do you mean?

00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:33.530
She never stays in one place for long,

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:36.330
but she causes tons of trouble.

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:38.180
Are you insulting her?

00:06:38.180 --> 00:06:39.730
Complimenting her.

00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:42.260
If I had that kind of sense of smell,

00:06:42.260 --> 00:06:44.070
I'd have been promoted by now.

00:06:45.560 --> 00:06:48.050
You seem to have the wrong 
idea, Higurashi-san.

00:06:49.560 --> 00:06:52.940
Whether she's helping someone or not,

00:06:52.940 --> 00:06:54.380
what she's doing is against the law.

00:06:54.950 --> 00:06:56.910
I cannot agree with it.

00:06:56.910 --> 00:06:59.670
So you want to catch her before she

00:06:59.670 --> 00:07:01.690
commits any more crimes.

00:07:01.990 --> 00:07:02.980
Yes.

00:07:03.370 --> 00:07:05.220
I probably shouldn't be saying this,

00:07:05.220 --> 00:07:08.490
but are you that set on 
throwing your master in jail?

00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:11.920
I want her to atone for her crimes.

00:07:11.920 --> 00:07:16.210
If in this era that 
means going to prison,

00:07:16.210 --> 00:07:17.750
I will send her there.

00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:20.440
I knew this already,

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:22.970
but you really are cold.

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:27.790
Supposedly she's a 
warring states general.

00:07:27.790 --> 00:07:29.500
Someone you know?

00:07:29.990 --> 00:07:32.400
Mogami Yoshiaki-sama.

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:34.790
But she was a rival of 
Masamune-sama's in the

00:07:34.790 --> 00:07:36.040
struggle for succession.

00:07:36.850 --> 00:07:39.770
So she didn't like Masamune-san.

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:40.700
Yes.

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:44.060
So I can't imagine 
she'd go to meet her.

00:07:44.470 --> 00:07:47.860
Yes, but if she's an 
enemy of Masamune,

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:50.250
then maybe she'll give us information.

00:07:50.850 --> 00:07:52.370
True.

00:07:52.370 --> 00:07:55.070
If she has any, that is.

00:07:57.450 --> 00:08:00.810
Thanks for waiting.
 Here's your coffee.

00:08:00.810 --> 00:08:02.750
Th-Thanks.

00:08:03.780 --> 00:08:05.080
I can't believe it!

00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:07.880
What are you thinking, Kojuro-san?!

00:08:08.290 --> 00:08:12.830
I thought you would be her ally, 
no matter what happened.

00:08:12.830 --> 00:08:17.400
But now you're working with 
the police to arrest her?

00:08:17.850 --> 00:08:19.700
But this is...

00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:20.710
Katakura.

00:08:22.280 --> 00:08:25.440
Looks like our information was bad.

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:28.800
Yes. But I wasn't lying to you.

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:31.740
I didn't think you were.

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:35.820
If you weren't lying then there's 
only one other possibility:

00:08:36.670 --> 00:08:41.270
her opinion of Masamune-san 
changed since she came here.

00:08:42.490 --> 00:08:43.970
Looks like you finally got it.

00:08:44.950 --> 00:08:47.460
She's met with Masamune.

00:08:47.970 --> 00:08:50.030
Then I'll...

00:08:50.030 --> 00:08:51.520
You stay quiet.

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:54.580
Yoshimitsu-chan, was it?

00:08:54.580 --> 00:08:56.330
Yoshiaki!

00:08:56.330 --> 00:08:58.180
Sorry, sorry.

00:08:58.180 --> 00:09:01.680
I don't know much about 
you or Katakura.

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:04.110
But I've followed her this far

00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:07.270
so I think I know a good 
deal about Masamune-san.

00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:09.360
But still you're planning

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:12.650
on arresting her with 
Kojuro-san, aren't you?

00:09:12.970 --> 00:09:16.130
Not at all. I'm not like her.

00:09:16.130 --> 00:09:18.300
I'm not going to arrest her.

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:19.700
Higurashi-san.

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:21.410
You shut up.

00:09:21.410 --> 00:09:22.160
Yes.

00:09:22.720 --> 00:09:27.790
True, according to our laws, 
she's done something wrong,

00:09:28.710 --> 00:09:31.550
but I don't think she's a bad person.

00:09:32.450 --> 00:09:34.310
You don't either, do you?

00:09:34.310 --> 00:09:35.050
Yeah.

00:09:35.330 --> 00:09:38.740
Then would you tell me what you know?

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:41.560
At this rate, she's going to be arrested

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:43.560
and thrown back in jail.

00:09:46.060 --> 00:09:49.870
I met her a while ago.

00:09:49.870 --> 00:09:52.820
In an old abandoned mansion 
I went to with some friends.

00:09:54.070 --> 00:09:57.030
Do you know where she went after that?

00:09:57.430 --> 00:09:59.990
I don't.

00:09:59.990 --> 00:10:03.450
She knocked me out and left 
without saying anything.

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:06.490
But you're worried about her anyway?

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:08.540
You're a kind girl.

00:10:09.990 --> 00:10:12.200
That's not true.

00:10:12.730 --> 00:10:15.630
Would you tell us where that 
place is, just in case?

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:17.550
You're willing to lie

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:20.180
with a straight face if it gets 
you information, aren't you?

00:10:21.810 --> 00:10:24.430
"I'm not like Katakura."

00:10:24.430 --> 00:10:26.020
I don't know how you could say that.

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:29.440
The two of us are acting out of 
different motives, aren't we?

00:10:29.760 --> 00:10:33.080
Actually, are you into little girls?

00:10:33.080 --> 00:10:34.560
You treated Yoshiaki-sama

00:10:34.560 --> 00:10:36.440
very differently than you treat me.

00:10:37.800 --> 00:10:41.790
Masamune-san's doing something bad 
and she's still very popular.

00:10:41.790 --> 00:10:45.240
And you're doing something 
good and nobody likes you.

00:10:45.820 --> 00:10:47.860
I'm accustomed to it.

00:10:50.590 --> 00:10:51.800
This is Higurashi.

00:10:51.800 --> 00:10:53.330
What is it chief?

00:10:55.470 --> 00:10:57.430
Yes. I'll be there soon.

00:10:57.430 --> 00:10:59.550
Katakura's with me, so she'll come, too.

00:10:59.550 --> 00:11:00.950
Did something happen?

00:11:01.520 --> 00:11:03.790
Masamune-san's been found.

00:11:03.790 --> 00:11:07.350
She's living in a fishing village 
in Kanezawa with two women.

00:11:07.830 --> 00:11:09.640
A Kanezawa fishing village?

00:11:10.710 --> 00:11:12.860
You look like you want 
to head straight there.

00:11:13.550 --> 00:11:15.760
I just don't want to lose her again.

00:11:16.530 --> 00:11:20.110
You really are cold.

00:11:26.230 --> 00:11:27.510
<i>I'm almost there.</i>

00:11:27.510 --> 00:11:30.370
<i>Wait there for me, Masamune-sama.</i>

00:11:31.050 --> 00:11:32.920
<i>I'm coming to arrest you.</i>

00:11:47.150 --> 00:11:49.510
Thank you for coming so far.

00:11:50.040 --> 00:11:51.560
I'm sure Masamune would be very happy.

00:11:51.980 --> 00:11:54.720
No, we're here for the investigation.

00:11:54.720 --> 00:11:58.620
Would you tell us about her?

00:11:58.620 --> 00:11:59.320
Yes.

00:11:59.990 --> 00:12:02.860
She loved to watch the sea.

00:12:02.860 --> 00:12:04.410
She would watch it all the time.

00:12:05.240 --> 00:12:07.190
Since she was on the 
run from the police,

00:12:07.190 --> 00:12:09.410
I told her to stop.

00:12:09.940 --> 00:12:11.290
But she wasn't the type to listen.

00:12:11.760 --> 00:12:12.930
I understand.

00:12:13.820 --> 00:12:16.350
She went to look at the 
sea yesterday, too.

00:12:16.350 --> 00:12:18.900
Takase-san found her there.

00:12:19.400 --> 00:12:20.530
Takase-san?

00:12:20.530 --> 00:12:22.800
The local policeman.

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:24.700
I see.

00:12:24.700 --> 00:12:28.460
And so she was running from him

00:12:28.460 --> 00:12:30.310
when she was chased to a cliff...

00:12:32.800 --> 00:12:34.940
And was shot and fell into the water.

00:12:34.940 --> 00:12:35.930
Yes.

00:12:40.470 --> 00:12:42.240
You look like you want 
to say something.

00:12:42.240 --> 00:12:43.930
Should I?

00:12:43.930 --> 00:12:45.830
You don't have to tell me.

00:12:46.610 --> 00:12:49.050
<i>Yes, you don't have to.</i>

00:12:49.740 --> 00:12:53.700
Katakura, would you look 
after Keiko-san for a while?

00:12:53.700 --> 00:12:54.840
Huh?

00:12:54.840 --> 00:12:57.210
I'm going to speak with the villagers.

00:12:57.210 --> 00:12:59.130
I'll go with you.

00:12:59.860 --> 00:13:01.820
I don't want anyone to think this is

00:13:01.820 --> 00:13:03.650
interfering with the job I'm doing.

00:13:03.650 --> 00:13:06.760
I guess you wouldn't 
understand, so I'll tell you.

00:13:06.760 --> 00:13:11.260
If the person you love dies, 
it hurts to be alone.

00:13:15.510 --> 00:13:17.230
I'm sorry, Katakura-san.

00:13:17.860 --> 00:13:20.070
I guess I'm interfering with your work.

00:13:20.430 --> 00:13:24.460
No. I apologize for 
Higurashi's rudeness.

00:13:26.140 --> 00:13:29.830
<i>I wish I could cry like her.</i>

00:13:30.540 --> 00:13:33.660
Um, Katakura-san, 
what's your full name?

00:13:34.030 --> 00:13:37.850
It's Katakura Kojuro, why do you ask?

00:13:38.840 --> 00:13:39.920
Kojuro...

00:13:41.010 --> 00:13:42.680
Got a second, Katakura?

00:13:43.320 --> 00:13:44.950
I'm fine.

00:13:44.950 --> 00:13:46.800
Yes, I'm all right now.

00:13:47.210 --> 00:13:48.810
Sorry for bothering you.

00:13:48.810 --> 00:13:51.970
I know it hurts, but this is our job.

00:13:52.570 --> 00:13:53.780
I know.

00:13:56.120 --> 00:13:57.570
I'll get to the point:

00:13:57.570 --> 00:14:00.650
there was nothing contradictory 
in the villagers' stories.

00:14:00.650 --> 00:14:03.690
Then did she really die?

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:06.030
It would seem so.

00:14:06.470 --> 00:14:07.820
Did they find the body?

00:14:08.540 --> 00:14:12.040
If you saw the place where 
it happened, you wouldn't ask.

00:14:12.040 --> 00:14:13.350
Did they?

00:14:13.350 --> 00:14:14.700
No.

00:14:14.700 --> 00:14:16.330
Of course they didn't.

00:14:16.920 --> 00:14:18.680
There's no way somebody could

00:14:18.680 --> 00:14:20.220
survive a fall off that cliff.

00:14:20.790 --> 00:14:22.810
The waters are below, 
but the currents are rough,

00:14:22.810 --> 00:14:24.240
too rough to swim.

00:14:24.880 --> 00:14:25.650
Then...

00:14:26.200 --> 00:14:28.490
Well, if warring states 
generals are made

00:14:28.490 --> 00:14:32.350
of metal stronger than those rocks,
 we might find her.

00:14:32.940 --> 00:14:35.100
You're a cold person.

00:14:35.860 --> 00:14:38.050
Normally, if a friend of yours died,

00:14:38.050 --> 00:14:40.130
you wouldn't ask if they found the body.

00:14:40.130 --> 00:14:41.420
You'd be too scared.

00:14:41.420 --> 00:14:44.110
Then should I not have?

00:14:44.710 --> 00:14:48.260
To be honest, no matter what you said,

00:14:48.260 --> 00:14:50.780
I believed that you were ready

00:14:50.780 --> 00:14:54.620
to betray me and run away with Masamune-san.

00:14:55.440 --> 00:14:58.010
Sorry I didn't live up 
to your expectations.

00:14:58.010 --> 00:15:01.330
You're disappointed that I'm only 
interested in my work, right?

00:15:01.690 --> 00:15:04.500
Yes. That's exactly right.

00:15:05.850 --> 00:15:08.510
I'm going to head back.

00:15:08.510 --> 00:15:09.600
What?

00:15:09.600 --> 00:15:12.090
We've been running around 
without any kind of rest.

00:15:12.640 --> 00:15:14.610
Masamune-san won't run anymore.

00:15:15.190 --> 00:15:16.600
There's no reason to hurry.

00:15:17.280 --> 00:15:18.280
Yes.

00:15:18.960 --> 00:15:21.980
May I go to the site while you rest?

00:15:22.220 --> 00:15:23.640
The site, huh?

00:15:23.640 --> 00:15:25.330
Yeah, that's important.

00:15:25.330 --> 00:15:27.760
I'll check it tomorrow.

00:15:27.760 --> 00:15:30.530
Yes. Good work today, Higurashi-san.

00:15:30.530 --> 00:15:32.620
You, too, Katakura.

00:16:09.840 --> 00:16:11.740
So Masamune-sama died here...

00:16:14.270 --> 00:16:17.910
Will you honestly not listen to a word I say?

00:16:21.130 --> 00:16:25.270
I'm sorry I wasn't a cute 
girl like Keiko-san.

00:16:26.520 --> 00:16:29.440
The only thing I care about is my work!

00:16:30.200 --> 00:16:33.280
I'm fine, even if you leave me alone!

00:16:44.040 --> 00:16:44.900
Kojuro.

00:16:46.760 --> 00:16:49.900
I didn't think you'd try and follow me.

00:16:54.410 --> 00:16:57.740
Masamune-sama, 
you're supposed to be dead...

00:17:01.570 --> 00:17:04.540
You're supposed to be dead... So why?

00:17:05.700 --> 00:17:09.090
You never cry when you're in pain.

00:17:10.160 --> 00:17:11.340
Yes.

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:15.340
I'm crying because I got to see you.

00:17:15.620 --> 00:17:16.560
I...

00:17:20.740 --> 00:17:23.240
But how are you?

00:17:23.240 --> 00:17:27.250
The villagers lied for me.

00:17:27.820 --> 00:17:32.150
If I'm dead, the police 
will stop looking for me.

00:17:34.440 --> 00:17:36.570
So you tricked everyone?

00:17:37.150 --> 00:17:39.590
So you could escape 
punishment for your crimes?

00:17:40.560 --> 00:17:42.830
True, it's not something 
to be proud of.

00:17:43.240 --> 00:17:44.740
Then why?

00:17:44.740 --> 00:17:49.360
I believed in you, that you'd 
never do something like that!

00:17:49.360 --> 00:17:51.630
It was because I wanted 
to apologize to you.

00:17:51.630 --> 00:17:54.050
Apologize to me?

00:17:54.630 --> 00:17:59.850
I couldn't be arrested 
until I apologized to you.

00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:03.350
I'm so very sorry, Kojuro.

00:18:03.940 --> 00:18:05.230
Masamune-sama?

00:18:05.230 --> 00:18:07.130
I was deceived by the Yakuza

00:18:07.130 --> 00:18:10.650
and damaged your reputation, 
as you were my instructor.

00:18:11.370 --> 00:18:12.380
You did.

00:18:13.320 --> 00:18:16.650
So I'd like to ask you 
again, knowing this.

00:18:17.020 --> 00:18:19.530
Please stay with me.

00:18:20.270 --> 00:18:23.440
Are you telling me to 
escape with a criminal?

00:18:23.900 --> 00:18:26.750
Do you think I'd let you do that?

00:18:27.110 --> 00:18:28.540
I know and I'm asking anyway.

00:18:29.250 --> 00:18:31.860
Asking despite knowing you 
wouldn't do anything that

00:18:31.860 --> 00:18:32.880
isn't upright and honest.

00:18:33.410 --> 00:18:35.860
You said you were going to apologize,

00:18:35.860 --> 00:18:37.420
but those were just words!

00:18:38.400 --> 00:18:41.720
I know it's wrong, 
but I can't change how I live.

00:18:42.230 --> 00:18:45.020
I can't change how I live either.

00:18:46.100 --> 00:18:49.690
But I also don't want to leave you.

00:18:49.690 --> 00:18:51.370
Is there nothing we can do?

00:18:52.100 --> 00:18:54.400
I don't know.

00:18:56.350 --> 00:18:57.240
Who's there?

00:18:58.650 --> 00:19:00.950
If you don't come out, 
I'll assume you're an enemy.

00:19:02.750 --> 00:19:04.270
Stylish...

00:19:04.270 --> 00:19:05.330
Hold on!

00:19:05.330 --> 00:19:06.520
Higurashi!

00:19:08.240 --> 00:19:09.960
You just attacked me?

00:19:09.960 --> 00:19:11.660
You're pretty riled up.

00:19:11.660 --> 00:19:14.470
Kojuro, do you know him?

00:19:14.470 --> 00:19:16.940
He's my superior in the police force.

00:19:16.940 --> 00:19:19.260
But, Higurashi-san, why?

00:19:19.590 --> 00:19:22.260
The villagers were cold.

00:19:23.560 --> 00:19:26.090
They seemed to be very grateful to you,

00:19:26.090 --> 00:19:28.730
but at the same time they held a 
funeral the day you fell off the cliff.

00:19:29.410 --> 00:19:32.230
That's not normal at all.

00:19:32.820 --> 00:19:37.530
So you let Kojuro go and 
waited for me to appear?

00:19:37.890 --> 00:19:42.300
I didn't expect you to bite 
the hook this soon, honestly.

00:19:43.270 --> 00:19:47.160
But you may not be able to reel me in.

00:19:47.830 --> 00:19:48.990
Come to think of it,

00:19:48.990 --> 00:19:50.960
I was rather rude the first time we met.

00:19:52.060 --> 00:19:56.760
I didn't know you were a princess.

00:19:57.790 --> 00:19:59.420
You're that detective?

00:19:59.900 --> 00:20:01.970
Both of us were ignorant.

00:20:01.970 --> 00:20:03.430
I don't blame you for that.

00:20:03.860 --> 00:20:08.050
However, if you intend to punish 
Kojuro as a traitor,

00:20:08.480 --> 00:20:09.930
I cannot ignore that.

00:20:17.290 --> 00:20:20.510
I'd rather tell my boss you got away

00:20:20.510 --> 00:20:23.900
than get killed trying to arrest you.

00:20:23.900 --> 00:20:26.460
But you said you'd do your job.

00:20:26.460 --> 00:20:28.870
That the warring states 
generals were your enemy...

00:20:28.870 --> 00:20:32.870
That's before I knew 
what they were like.

00:20:33.410 --> 00:20:35.990
Masamune-san died when 
she fell off the cliff.

00:20:36.600 --> 00:20:38.900
And so you quit WarGen.

00:20:39.600 --> 00:20:41.260
That's what I'll tell them.

00:20:42.050 --> 00:20:43.060
But...

00:20:43.560 --> 00:20:47.280
If you still don't like that, 
then I'll give you an order:

00:20:47.850 --> 00:20:51.280
stay by her side and watch her forever.

00:20:54.150 --> 00:20:56.910
If it's an order I don't have a choice.

00:20:56.910 --> 00:21:01.390
The job's too much of a pain 
to leave to anybody else.

00:21:04.580 --> 00:21:07.890
Sorry I said you were a cold.

00:21:08.870 --> 00:21:12.000
You're pretty when you smile.

00:21:13.180 --> 00:21:16.100
D-Don't be weird.

00:21:16.100 --> 00:21:18.460
That's sexual harassment.

00:21:20.600 --> 00:21:24.430
Anyway, I'm tired, 
so I'm going back to the hotel.

00:21:25.610 --> 00:21:29.930
Are you sure about going with me?

00:21:31.010 --> 00:21:32.610
Masamune-sama!

00:21:34.040 --> 00:21:37.750
The only one I want to be with is you.

00:21:38.280 --> 00:21:40.380
Is that a problem?

00:21:41.980 --> 00:21:45.230
Not a problem, 
and I'm not worried at all.

00:21:46.220 --> 00:21:47.320
Now then...

00:21:47.320 --> 00:21:48.820
What should we do?

00:21:49.600 --> 00:21:53.560
For now, I'd like to get away 
from this dangerous place.

00:21:54.140 --> 00:21:54.870
Yeah.

00:21:57.020 --> 00:21:59.460
M-Masamune-sama?

00:22:00.130 --> 00:22:01.470
Where do you want to go?

00:22:02.500 --> 00:22:06.180
Anywhere you go...

00:22:07.240 --> 00:22:09.260
Thank you, Kojuro.

00:23:46.460 --> 00:23:49.530
Next time is the Dune, 
Amago Tsunehisa-dono!

00:23:49.990 --> 00:23:53.460
Next time on Sengoku 
Collection: "The Dune!"

00:23:54.770 --> 00:23:57.030
These previews are always so random!

00:23:57.030 --> 00:23:58.610
We should do them properly!
